cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  VisionGuard: a research platform for measuring adversarial
  robustness of embedding-based image retrieval
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dawid
    family-names: Cybulski
    alias: cybulskydavid
repository-code: 'https://github.com/cybulskydavid/vision-guard'
abstract: >-
  VisionGuard is a modular experiment platform for studying how
  adversarial perturbations degrade image retrieval systems built on
  frozen vision foundation models. It re-derives the FGSM, PGD and
  Carlini-Wagner attacks to operate on embedding geometry rather than
  class labels, and evaluates CLIP and DINO backbones on CUB-200-2011,
  Stanford Cars and Stanford Online Products under raw, PCA-compressed
  and metric-learning (Triplet, ArcFace) embedding heads. Retrieval
  quality is measured with leave-one-out Recall@1 and mAP, reported as
  mean and standard deviation across multiple independent seeds.
  The platform is the engineering follow-up to the author's master's
  thesis on the same research question, generalised into reusable,
  reproducible infrastructure.
keywords:
  - adversarial-robustness
  - adversarial-attacks
  - image-retrieval
  - metric-learning
  - representation-learning
  - vision-foundation-models
  - clip
  - dino
  - pytorch
license: MIT

